  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jackson Merrill's power gave them early cushion, but it took Sung-Mun Song's ninth-inning single to finish this game the way it needed to end.",
    "what_this_means": "The Padres got what they required from a day game in St. Louis: early command from Rodriguez, a bullpen that held after he exited, and a lineup that converted runners on base when it mattered. Merrill drove in two with his home run in the opening innings, setting the tone before the game tightened. They never trailed, never gave ground, and when the eighth inning passed without damage, they got one more chance. Song sparked the three-run ninth, turning what looked like a comfortable lead into something that felt complete. The win is clean on paper. The execution was fragile. They left runners on base in the sixth and eighth before finding that one breakthrough moment late. This is a team that doesn't waste extra chances once they arrive.",
    "what_to_watch": "Texas sends an undetermined starter tomorrow night. The Rangers hit .218 as a team this season. Randy V\u00e1squez takes the ball for the Padres against an offense that has not solved anything at the plate.",
